WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.820
Good Morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:02.660
It's question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:04.360
from real nerdfighters, let's get right to it!

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.980
What's your least favorite kind of animal?

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.500
Mice who lord over theme parks.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.240
What's your favorite dance move?

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.780
This one. You take this guys up and then OH, you're dancing.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.540
I'm dancing. &lt;Hits printer with leg&gt; OW.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.700
I wanna apologise to my printer.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.700
Why does everyone like ferrets so much?

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.740
I don't know who you're hanging out with, but that is not an issue in my house.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.320
What's your favorite photograph?

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.700
This one, called "Young farmers", also sometimes known as "Three farmers on their way to a dance, August 1914".

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.380
There were two dances that they were on their way to, of course, the one they knew about and

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.340
World War I. How's Willy?

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.620
He's good. Here, you can watch him for the next several questions.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:43.060
TFiOS casting?! Yes, Ansel Elgort has been cast as Augustus Waters and Hazel Grace Lancaster will be

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.280
played by Shailene Woodley.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.160
But I am a GIANT SQUID OF ANGER about this!! Yeah, that's not a question but I am grateful that you are

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.300
passionate about the book and want it to be a good movie but you have to understand-

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:57.600
I ALSO want it to be a good movie and I've actually seen the auditions and you aren't going to

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.220
think "Oh, that's Shailene Woodley" or "Oh, that's the guy who plays Caleb Prior in Divergent",

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.940
you're just gonna think "Oh, that's Hazel and Gus".

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.180
How much say do you actually have in casting?

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:11.320
A surprising amount. I mean, I'm definitely not casting the movie but the producers and the director

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.440
have been really really nice about including me in everything!

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.220
What did you think of the Gatsby movie? &lt;frustrated sigh&gt;

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.780
Hey, what would you do if you were invisible for an hour?

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:24.280
I would go to the emergency room. I mean, I'm pretty hypochondriacal but I assume that anyone who

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:28.560
suddenly became invisible would proceed with some haste to the nearest healthcare provider and be like,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.820
"Why am I invisible?! I Googled it but there is nothing in the medical literature. Perhaps we should do a CAT scan!"

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.660
How many times a day do you check your cellphone?

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.040
I'm sorry, what's that?

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.300
Are you good at multitasking?

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:44.340
Studies consistently show that the better people think they are at multitasking, the worse they actually are and

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.760
I am GREAT at it.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.120
How does it feel to be a doctor?

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.960
About the same as it felt before, actually.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.320
Did they let you keep your cape thing?

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:55.380
DID they? I've hardly taken it off. By the way, it is technically known as a cape thing.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.320
Would you rather fight a rabid badger or Nicholas Cage?

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.760
Well, I'm gonna have to know more about the badger - is it a regular badger or a honey badger?

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:07.460
Is it like a baby badger? If it's a regular baby badger, I'm gonna take the rabid badger. Otherwise,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.740
definitely Nick Cage.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:11.920
If you could only recommend one book to nerdfighteria, what would it be?

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:17.780
Well, that changes weekly. At the moment, my recommendation for zombie novels is "The End Games" but T. Michel Martin, for non-zombie

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.900
novels, I'm gonna recommend "How To Get Filthy Rich In Rising Asia"

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.680
If I were to gift you a pegasus, what color would you like it to be?

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.100
Listen, that's very nice of you but I do not want a pegasus. First, there's the fact that I don't have

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:32.560
a barn in which to house a pegasus. Also, there's the not insignificant cost of hay.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.140
Plus, I've always found flying pets to be kind of more trouble than they're worth.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.800
Hey, where do the ducks go when the pond freezes over?

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:44.120
They migrate South. EXCEPT in the actual case of Holden Caulfield, wondering what happens

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.840
to the ducks in the central park pond. They do not migrate South because the pond never freezes over.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.760
As the official photographer for central park put it "I don't know what Salinger was thinking. I've worked at the park

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.400
for 27 years and I've always seen ducks in the winter."

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.220
Have you ever been tempted to get nerdfighters to tame honey badgers so you could have a Broadway musical

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:06.140
starring honey badgers? Yeah, I can see the headline now "Man convinces children to tame honey

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:11.160
badgers for strange Broadway musical. 7 dead, including no honey badgers."

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.240
Hank, D.F.T.B.A, I will see you on Friday.

